## Purpose
- Give fast operational commands for local bring-up and smoke checks.

## Source of truth
- `aspire/TeamHub.AppHost/Program.cs`
- `docker-compose.yml` (shared base)
- `docker-compose.dev.yml` (Aspire companion overrides — monitoring only; use `scripts/compose-dev.sh`)
- `docker-compose.staging.yml` (full-stack staging overlay; localhost binds)
- `.env.dev.example` / `.env.staging.example`
- `scripts/compose-dev.sh` / `scripts/compose-staging.sh`
- `frontend/team-hub-web/package.json`
- `infrastructure/monitoring/docker-compose.monitoring.yml`
- `infrastructure/monitoring/otel-collector-config.yaml`
- `infrastructure/monitoring/tempo.yaml`
- `infrastructure/monitoring/prometheus.yml`
- `infrastructure/monitoring/prometheus.dev.yml`

## Do
- **Preferred local dev (full stack, one command):**
  - prerequisites: .NET 10 SDK, Aspire 13 (`Aspire.AppHost.Sdk` via NuGet), Docker, Node.js/npm
  - `cd aspire/TeamHub.AppHost && dotnet run`
  - opens Aspire Dashboard (URL in console); endpoints: frontend `https://localhost:4200`, nginx API `https://localhost:8080`, gateway `http://localhost:5000`
  - JWT dev config: `aspire/TeamHub.AppHost/appsettings.Development.json` (`Aspire:Jwt:*`)
  - stop with `Ctrl+C` in AppHost terminal
- **Optional monitoring next to Aspire:**
  - `cp .env.dev.example .env.dev` (set `GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD`)
  - `./scripts/compose-dev.sh up -d` (merges `infrastructure/monitoring/docker-compose.monitoring.yml` + `docker-compose.dev.yml`)
  - project `team-hub-dev` — Grafana/Loki/Tempo/Prometheus/OTel only (Aspire owns Postgres/Redis/Kafka/Azurite/apps)
  - Prometheus uses `prometheus.dev.yml` (`host.docker.internal:5000`–`5004`); nginx exporter scrapes `host.docker.internal:8081`
  - AppHost OTLP → `http://127.0.0.1:4317`; edge logs shared via `infrastructure/monitoring/.nginx-edge-logs`
- **Demo seed via Aspire** (Development; auth → org → notification inbox for JanWilk):
  - `cd aspire/TeamHub.AppHost && dotnet run -- --seed` (or `dotnet run --launch-profile seed`)
  - AppHost exits when `seed-notification` Finished; login `JanWilk123` / `janwilk123` (Owner of `demo-org-1`)
  - re-seed: remove Aspire Postgres named volume, then run `--seed` again
  - details: `aspire/AGENT.md`
- **Staging full stack (Docker):**
  - `./scripts/setup-certs.sh` (mkcert = trusted HTTPS in browser; otherwise self-signed with warning)
  - `cp .env.staging.example .env.staging` and replace every `CHANGE_ME` (JWT ≥ 32 chars, Postgres password, Grafana password)
  - `./scripts/compose-staging.sh up --build -d`
  - equivalent: `docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.staging.yml --env-file .env.staging up --build -d`
  - project `team-hub-staging`; containers use `ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production`
  - published ports bind to `127.0.0.1` only (see `docker-compose.staging.yml`); apps use `restart: unless-stopped`
  - `gw-api` healthcheck required before `gw-nginx` starts (`service_healthy`)
- TLS certs are shared from `./certs` into `ui-web` and `gw-nginx` containers.
- Use `https://localhost:4200`, `https://localhost:8080` (API edge), and `http://localhost:5000` (gateway debug).
- Compose secrets live in root `.env.dev` / `.env.staging` (gitignored); never commit them.
- Expected host ports after staging start (all on loopback):
  - frontend `https://localhost:4200` (`ui-web-staging`)
  - infrastructure nginx `https://localhost:8080` (`gw-nginx-staging`, API entry)
  - gateway `http://localhost:5000` (`gw-api-staging`, debug only)
  - auth (direct) `http://localhost:5001` (`srv-auth-staging`); health `GET http://localhost:5001/health`
  - redis `localhost:6379` (`cache-redis-staging`)
  - postgres `localhost:5433` (`db-postgres-staging`, databases `authdb` + `organizationdb` + `notificationdb`)
  - Azurite blob `localhost:10000` (`blob-storage-staging`)
  - monitoring Grafana `http://localhost:3000`
  - monitoring Loki `http://localhost:3100`
  - monitoring Tempo `http://localhost:3200`
  - monitoring Prometheus `http://localhost:9090`
  - monitoring OTel Collector OTLP gRPC `localhost:4317`, HTTP `localhost:4318`
- Optional standalone Redis (without root compose):
  - `cp infrastructure/redis/.env.example infrastructure/redis/.env`
  - `docker compose -f infrastructure/redis/docker-compose.redis.yml --env-file infrastructure/redis/.env up -d`
- Optional standalone monitoring (without root compose):
  - `cp infrastructure/monitoring/.env.example infrastructure/monitoring/.env`
  - `docker compose -f infrastructure/monitoring/docker-compose.monitoring.yml --env-file infrastructure/monitoring/.env up -d`
  - Grafana: `http://localhost:3000` (credentials from env file)
  - Loki ready check: `GET http://localhost:3100/ready`
- First telemetry in Grafana (OTLP via collector):
  - start staging stack (or Aspire + `./scripts/compose-dev.sh up -d`)
  - generate traffic: `curl http://localhost:5000/health` (gateway) or `curl http://localhost:5001/health` (auth)
  - metrics scrape check: `curl http://localhost:5001/metrics | head`
  - open Grafana `http://localhost:3000` (credentials from `.env.dev` / `.env.staging`)
  - Explore -> **Loki** -> `{service_name="team-hub-auth"}` or `{service_name="team-hub-gateway"}`
  - Explore -> **Tempo** -> search by TraceId from `X-Correlation-ID` response header
  - Explore -> **Prometheus** -> `http_server_request_duration_seconds_count`
  - note: staging logs are pushed via OTLP (not Docker stdout scraping); Aspire/`dotnet run` logs stay local unless OTLP endpoint is reachable
- Quick auth smoke through infrastructure nginx:
  - `POST https://localhost:8080/api/auth/register`
  - `POST https://localhost:8080/api/auth/login`
  - `POST https://localhost:8080/api/auth/refresh` (with cookie)
  - `POST https://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout`
- Quick auth smoke through gateway (debug):
  - `POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/register`
  - `POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login`
  - `POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/refresh` (with cookie)
  - `POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/logout`
- Quick auth smoke through frontend nginx proxy:
  - `POST https://localhost:4200/api/auth/register`
- Debug staging request by Correlation ID:
  - reproduce in UI and copy `X-Correlation-ID` from browser DevTools (Network tab, request or response headers)
  - or call API directly and read response header: `curl -s -D - -o /dev/null -H "X-Correlation-ID: test-id" http://localhost:5000/health`
  - open Grafana `http://localhost:3000` -> Explore -> Loki
  - query both services: `{service_name=~"team-hub-gateway|team-hub-auth"} | json | CorrelationId="<trace-id>"`
  - gateway proxy lines include `CorrelationId` in structured log; auth request logs include the same field
  - if log lines look like `[09:14:47 INF] team_hub_auth...` (plain text), the container is not using Production Serilog JSON — rebuild with `./scripts/compose-staging.sh up --build srv-auth gw-api` and confirm `ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production`
  - in Grafana, use `| json` to extract `CorrelationId`; plain-text log lines do not show structured fields in the message body
- Health checks (reduce Grafana/console noise):
  - auth / organization / notification / bff / gateway Docker healthcheck interval is `120s` (`docker-compose.yml` + Dockerfiles)
  - `gw-nginx` waits for `gw-api` `service_healthy`
  - `/health` and `/metrics` requests are excluded from Serilog request logging in gateway and auth
  - gateway logs `/health` only when unhealthy

## Don't
- Do not keep secrets in committed `.env*.example` files or repo root tracked env files.
- Do not use staging Compose for daily local dev when Aspire AppHost is available.
- Do not start Aspire AppHost and staging Compose on the same host ports at once.
- Do not expect `docker-compose.dev.yml` alone to start monitoring or Postgres/Redis/Kafka — use `./scripts/compose-dev.sh`; Aspire owns app infra for local dev.
- Do not run heavy builds/tests for docs-only updates.
- Do not verify auth flow by bypassing gateway when checking end-to-end.

## Checklist
- Containers healthy (`db-postgres-staging`, `srv-auth-staging`, `srv-organization-staging`, `gw-api-staging`, `gw-nginx-staging`, `ui-web-staging`).
- Gateway route `/api/auth/*` reaches auth service.
- Frontend can authenticate with cookie-based refresh flow.
